===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|savoury}} {{qualifier|British; usually only for etymology 1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-savory.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{IPA|/ˈseɪvəɹi/|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From the {{inh|en|enm|savory}}, {{m|enm|savourie}}, from {{der|en|fro|savouré}}, from {{der|en|fro|savourer}}, from {{der|en|LL.|sapōrāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|sapōrō}}, from {{der|en|la|sapor|t=taste, flavor}}, from {{m|la|sapio|sapiō, sapere|taste of, have a flavor of}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|savorier}} {{tcx|American spelling|lang=en}}

# [[tasty|Tasty]], attractive to the [[palate]].
#: ''The fine restaurant presented an array of '''savory''' dishes; each was delicious.''
# [[salty|Salty]] and/or [[spicy]], but not sweet.
#: ''The mushrooms, meat, bread, rice, peanuts and potatoes were all good '''savory''' foods.''
#: ''The '''savory''' duck contrasted well with the sweet sauce.''
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Morally or ethically [[acceptable]].
#: ''Readers are to be warned that quotations in this chapter contain some not so '''savory''' language.''

=====Synonyms=====
* See also [[Thesaurus:delicious]]

